text:
This looks like an arugula salad with a light dressing, a few pine nuts, and maybe some bits of pepper. It sits on a square plate roughly 24 cm across. The greens form a loose pile, so I estimate about 60-70 g of greens. The dressing and nuts add a little more weight, which brings the total to about 75 g.

For energy, arugula is about 25 kcal per 100 g, so roughly 17 kcal for the greens. Dressing at about 1 tbsp of oil adds around 80 kcal, and a few pine nuts add around 20 kcal. That comes to about 120 kcal.

